# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — added when this project joined the Vesopa-Ltd umbrella repo
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SIGNING KEYS ARE THE MOST DANGEROUS FILES IN THIS PROJECT.
#
# A leaked Android signing key lets anyone build an APK that Android accepts as
# a genuine Vesopa update, and unlike a password it CANNOT be rotated: every
# device with the app installed is pinned to that key for the life of the app.
# A new key means a new listing and no upgrade path for existing users.
#
# They were untracked but unignored, which meant the next `git add -A` in this
# repo would have published them.
*.key
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
key.properties
keystore.properties
keys/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
*service-account*.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows desktop build output
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CMake caches, Visual Studio workspace state and compiled objects. Regenerated
# by every build, and `cmake.db` and `CMakeCache.txt` carry absolute paths from
# whichever machine last compiled — so they conflict on every pull for no gain.
windows/runner/out/
windows/runner/.vs/
windows/flutter/ephemeral/
